sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/scaling-bending-law> dct:description "Proof scope of the kernel-checked statement recorded as scaling-bending-law: 2 statement(s) the Lean kernel checked and 3 assumption(s) stated in the module header and not proved." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Kernel-checked: R9a: with CubeLaw F, LeverLaw ℓ and SectionModulusLaw Z, σ_b(L2)/σ_b(L1) = L2/L1, log exponent 1 (bendingStress_ratio_body, bendingStress_log_body); σ_max/σ_b = σ_max k_Z/(k_F k_ℓ L) (bendingSafety_eq); above σ_max k_Z/(k_F k_ℓ n) the stress at n times the load exceeds σ_max (bending_cannot_carry)." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Kernel-checked: R9b: with AreaLaw F instead, σ_b(L2)/σ_b(L1) = 1, log exponent 0 (bendingStress_ratio_sheet, bendingStress_log_sheet): no size limit follows." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Assumed, not proved: Slender linear-elastic (Euler-Bernoulli) beam; σ_b = M_b/Z with a point load at the free end (a distributed load changes the constant, not the L-dependence)." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Assumed, not proved: Geometrically similar sections (Z = k_Z d^3, d ∝ L) and lever arm ∝ L; elastic similarity (d ∝ ℓ^(3/2)) is a different hypothesis family, not formalised." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Assumed, not proved: Constant σ_max; static loads only (wind on a leaf is outside the model); which load family applies (R9a or R9b) is empirical and must be committed by the candidate." ;
    rdfs:comment "The kernel-checked statements are theorems of the model; the assumptions are the model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it. The assumptions it rests on, written in the module header and never proved, are: Slender linear-elastic (Euler-Bernoulli) beam; σ_b = M_b/Z with a point load at the free end (a distributed load changes the constant, not the L-dependence); Geometrically similar sections (Z = k_Z d^3, d ∝ L) and lever arm ∝ L; elastic similarity (d ∝ ℓ^(3/2)) is a different hypothesis family, not formalised; Constant σ_max; static loads only (wind on a leaf is outside the model); which load family applies (R9a or R9b) is empirical and must be committed by the candidate. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the source is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/Delphi/Scaling.lean> .
}

